# Guilds Structured Reference

This file reorganizes guild and guardian knowledge into the same keyed mechanic format used by other deterministic knowledge sources.
The original raw source remains preserved in public/knowledge/guilds for side-by-side comparison.

Mechanic: Guilds
Type: System
Domain: Social Progression
Section: Guilds
Category: Social
Aliases: none.
Definition: Guilds are a seasonal social progression system that grants shared participation rewards, guild-shop access, and guardians.
Behavior:
Guilds unlock at Milestone Tier 3 Wave 10.
Players can join an existing guild or create their own guild.
Each guild supports up to 30 players.
Joining a guild opens guild rewards, guild-shop purchases, and guardians.

Mechanic: Guild Creation
Type: Access Rule
Domain: Guilds
Section: Guilds
Category: Membership
Aliases: create guild
Definition: Guild Creation lets a player found a new guild with its own setup and join rules.
Behavior:
Creating a guild costs 50 gems.
The creator chooses the guild name, description, and icon.
Join policy can be Free, With Approval, or Invitation Only.

Mechanic: Guild Joining
Type: Access Rule
Domain: Guilds
Section: Guilds
Category: Membership
Aliases: join guild
Definition: Guild Joining is the process of finding a guild and entering it under that guild's join rules.
Behavior:
Players can search the available guild list and request to join shown guilds.
Free guilds allow immediate entry.
With Approval guilds require leader approval.
Invitation Only guilds do not appear in the public guild list.

Mechanic: Guild Rewards
Type: Reward System
Domain: Guilds
Section: Guilds
Category: Rewards
Aliases: guild reward rules
Definition: Guild Rewards are the recurring resource payouts and unlocks tied to guild participation.
Behavior:
Joining a guild gives access to guardians.
Guild contribution is earned from Weekly Challenge boxes.
Coin reward scales from the player's highest unlocked tier.
Players can reference Daily Missions to see their base coin reward.

Mechanic: Guild Contribution
Type: Progress Metric
Domain: Guilds
Section: Guilds
Category: Rewards
Aliases: contribution
Definition: Guild Contribution is the weekly participation total used to unlock guild reward chests.
Behavior:
Guild contribution is earned from Weekly Challenge boxes.
Weekly reward chest breakpoints are 100, 250, 500, and 750 contribution.
Higher contribution unlocks more tokens, bits, coins, and gems.

Mechanic: Guild Weekly Reward Chests
Type: Reward Table
Domain: Guilds
Section: Guilds
Category: Rewards
Aliases: weekly guild chests; guild chest rewards
Definition: Guild Weekly Reward Chests are the four contribution-based payout tiers for guild participation.
Behavior:
100 contribution gives 10 tokens, 10 bits, 1x coins, and 5 gems.
250 contribution gives 20 tokens, 25 bits, 2x coins, and 10 gems.
500 contribution gives 40 tokens, 50 bits, 3x coins, and 15 gems.
750 contribution gives 80 tokens, 100 bits, 5x coins, and 30 gems.
Claiming all four chests totals 150 tokens, 185 bits, 11x coins, and 60 gems.

Mechanic: Guild Seasons
Type: Seasonal Rule
Domain: Guilds
Section: Guilds
Category: Seasons
Aliases: guild season
Definition: Guild Seasons are the repeating time window that controls guild shops, guild themes, and token carryover.
Behavior:
Each guild season lasts 8 weeks.
Guild-shop purchase ladders reset at the beginning of the next season.
Guild themes rotate by season and can be missed.
Unused guild tokens are resolved through guild token cashout when the season ends.

Mechanic: Guild Token Cashout
Type: Conversion Rule
Domain: Guilds
Section: Guilds
Category: Seasons
Aliases: token cashout; token conversion
Definition: Guild Token Cashout converts leftover guild tokens into gems automatically when a guild season ends.
Behavior:
Unspent guild tokens convert to gems at a 5 to 1 ratio.
The result rounds up to the next whole gem.
Five guild tokens become one gem.
Cashout happens automatically at the end of each 8-week guild season.

Mechanic: Guild Shop
Type: Store
Domain: Guilds
Section: Guilds
Category: Purchases
Aliases: guild store
Definition: Guild Shop is the seasonal store that spends guild tokens on currencies, cosmetics, relics, and guardian-chip unlocks.
Behavior:
Guild shop purchases spend guild tokens.
The shop offers currencies, themes, relics, and chips.
Currency purchase ladders reset at the start of the next guild season.

Mechanic: Guild Shop Currency Purchases
Type: Cost Ladder
Domain: Guild Tokens
Section: Guilds
Category: Purchases
Aliases: guild currency costs; guild shop costs
Definition: Guild Shop Currency Purchases are the seasonal token ladders for bits, gems, and shards.
Behavior:
Currencies available are bits, gems, and shards.
Guild-token exchange gives 100 gems or 250 shards.
There are four shard types, and only the purchased shard type increases in cost.
Each listed currency purchase is capped at three buys per season.
Costs:
Bits cost 25, 50, and 75 tokens for purchases one through three.
Gems cost 15, 25, and 40 tokens for purchases one through three.
Shards cost 5, 10, and 15 tokens for purchases one through three.

Mechanic: Guild Themes
Type: Cosmetic Rotation
Domain: Guilds
Section: Guilds
Category: Purchases
Aliases: guild skins; seasonal themes
Definition: Guild Themes are seasonal cosmetic purchases sold in the guild shop and kept permanently once bought.
Behavior:
Themes rotate every guild season and may be missed.
One tower theme costs 100 tokens.
One background theme costs 100 tokens.
One menu theme costs 100 tokens.
One guardian skin costs 150 tokens.
Purchased themes remain available forever.

Mechanic: Guild Relics
Type: Limited Purchase
Domain: Guilds
Section: Guilds
Category: Purchases
Aliases: guild relics
Definition: Guild Relics are limited relic purchases sold through the guild shop at seasonal token price points.
Behavior:
Guild relics are sold at 75-token and 150-token price points.
Guild relics may be limited to the event that sponsors them.
Guild relic offers can be seasonal or time-limited.

Mechanic: Guardians
Type: Companion System
Domain: Guilds
Section: Guilds
Category: Guardians
Aliases: guardian system
Definition: Guardians are temporary-bonus guild companions with upgradeable chip stats and unlockable chip slots.
Behavior:
Joining a guild gives access to guardians.
Guardians are similar to bots and provide temporary bonuses while active.
Guardian chip slots can be unlocked up to four total.
Guardian chip upgrades cost bits.

Mechanic: Guardian Chips
Type: Upgrade System
Domain: Guardians
Section: Guilds
Category: Guardians
Aliases: guardian upgrades; guardian chips
Definition: Guardian Chips are the guardian abilities and upgrade lines that define each guardian's effect, cooldown, and secondary stat.
Behavior:
Ally and Attack unlock when guardians unlock.
Bounty, Fetch, Scout, and Summon are purchased in the guild shop for 200 tokens each.
Guardian chip upgrades cost bits.
Each guardian has three core upgrade stats with separate level caps and cost ladders.

Mechanic: Attack Guardian
Type: Guardian Chip
Domain: Guardians
Section: Guilds
Category: Guardian
Aliases: Attack
Definition: Attack Guardian attacks nearby enemies and deals damage equal to a percentage of the damage they have already taken.
Behavior:
Its three upgrade stats are Percentage, Cooldown, and Targets.
Base values are Percentage 1%, Cooldown 120s, and Targets 1.
Higher levels raise Percentage, reduce Cooldown, and increase Targets until each stat reaches its own cap.

Mechanic: Ally Guardian
Type: Guardian Chip
Domain: Guardians
Section: Guilds
Category: Guardian
Aliases: Ally
Definition: Ally Guardian converts an enemy into an ally recovery package that can heal the tower beyond basic maximum recovery.
Behavior:
Its three upgrade stats are Recovery Amount, Max Recovery, and Cooldown.
Base values are Recovery Amount 1%, Max Recovery x1.1, and Cooldown 120s.
Higher levels increase healing values and reduce Cooldown until each stat reaches its own cap.

Mechanic: Bounty Guardian
Type: Guardian Chip
Domain: Guardians
Section: Guilds
Category: Guardian
Aliases: Bounty
Definition: Bounty Guardian places a bounty on nearby non-common enemies so they grant more coins on death.
Behavior:
Its three upgrade stats are Multiplier, Cooldown, and Targets.
Base values are Multiplier x0.01, Cooldown 120s, and Targets 1.
Higher levels raise Multiplier, reduce Cooldown, and increase Targets until each stat reaches its own cap.

Mechanic: Fetch Guardian
Type: Guardian Chip
Domain: Guardians
Section: Guilds
Category: Guardian
Aliases: Fetch
Definition: Fetch Guardian locates and retrieves hidden loot such as coins, gems, medals, shards, and modules.
Behavior:
Its three upgrade stats are Cooldown, Find Chance, and Double Find Chance.
Base values are Cooldown 120s, Find Chance 10%, and Double Find Chance 2%.
Higher levels reduce Cooldown and improve both loot-find stats until each stat reaches its own cap.

Mechanic: Scout Guardian
Type: Guardian Chip
Domain: Guardians
Section: Guilds
Category: Guardian
Aliases: Scout
Definition: Scout Guardian treats enemies as being farther from the tower for damage calculations while the guardian is active.
Behavior:
Its three upgrade stats are Cooldown, Range Bonus, and Duration.
Base values are Cooldown 105s, Range Bonus x2.0, and Duration 5s.
Scout Guardian was introduced in Guild Season 7.
Higher levels reduce Cooldown and increase both Range Bonus and Duration until each stat reaches its own cap.

Mechanic: Summon Guardian
Type: Guardian Chip
Domain: Guardians
Section: Guilds
Category: Guardian
Aliases: Summon
Definition: Summon Guardian creates extra basic, ranged, tank, and fast enemies while active and applies a cash bonus to enemies during the summon window.
Behavior:
Its three upgrade stats are Duration, Cooldown, and Cash Bonus.
Base values are Duration 5s, Cooldown 140s, and Cash Bonus x1.00.
Summoned enemies cannot become Ultimate from a battle condition.
Higher levels extend Duration, reduce Cooldown, and increase Cash Bonus until each stat reaches its own cap.
